.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt UUENCODE 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uuencode
.Nd encode a binary file as POSIX uuencode text
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar input
.Ar output_name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads
.Ar input
(or standard input when omitted) and writes a
.Ql begin
line containing the file mode and
.Ar output_name ,
45-byte encoded body lines, a backtick terminator and an
.Ql end
line.
.Pp
The encoded output is written to standard output.
The encoded file name is stored in the header; it is not an output path.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A missing input or usage error exits nonzero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uudecode 1 ,
.Xr ar 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the POSIX uuencode format.
